BeatBox
=======

A music player for GNOME/GTK: library, playlists and smart playlists,
Cover Flow and a cover grid, podcasts, internet radio and iPod sync.

This is a fork of BeatBox by Scott Ringwelski and contributors
(originally at https://launchpad.net/beat-box, later continued as Noise).
The original project is no longer maintained. In 2026 it was ported to
meson, GTK3, GStreamer 1.0, libgee-0.8, libsoup-3 and Granite 6, and given
a new look, Cover Flow, an inline cover grid, podcast and radio directories,
online album art and skins.

License: GPL version 3 (see COPYING); the sources are "GPL version 2 or
later". Original authors and the fork's changes are listed in AUTHORS.

Building
--------

Dependencies (Arch): vala meson gtk3 granite libgee gstreamer gst-plugins-base
gst-plugins-good taglib libxml2 libnotify libsoup3 json-glib libgpod sqlite

    meson setup build
    ninja -C build
    ./build/beatbox

It runs straight from the build directory (translations included); on first
start it registers a launcher in ~/.local/share/applications so the desktop
shows its icon. `ninja -C build install` installs it system-wide instead.

Files
-----

- Library: ~/.local/share/beatbox/beatbox.db
- Options: ~/.config/beatbox/beatbox.conf
- Skins: folders in ~/.local/share/beatbox/skins (see skins/README.md)
- Look: data/theme.css (embedded in the binary)

Missing album art is looked up in MusicBrainz / the Cover Art Archive and the
Apple Music catalogue (Preferences > Covers); internet radio stations come
from radio-browser.info.

Versioning
----------

Each commit after the v0.8 tag is 0.8.N. To bump it automatically:

    ln -s ../../tools/pre-commit .git/hooks/pre-commit
